From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:08:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] -iwad, Freedoom, XDG config and savegame directories

- -iwad <file>: the game mode comes from the WAD's own lump directory
  (MAP01 -> commercial, E4M1 -> retail, E2M1 -> registered).
- With none of id's IWADs found, use Freedoom from DOOMWADDIR or the
  usual system locations.
- Config in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/psdoom/og.cfg, savegames in
  $XDG_DATA_HOME/psdoom/og/ (psDooM used ~/.psdoom, linuxdoom the cwd).
---
 linuxdoom-1.10/d_main.c   | 111 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 linuxdoom-1.10/doomstat.h |   1 +
 linuxdoom-1.10/g_game.c   |   2 +-
 linuxdoom-1.10/m_menu.c   |   4 +-
 4 files changed, 113 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

